IO-57: count runoff routed onto another subcatchment once in the system runoff

postOutputSnapshot() summed every subcatchment's runoff into sys_runoff (and
so into the system total lateral inflow), including subcatchments whose outlet
is another subcatchment, whose runoff already contains that runon. Apply the
rule the runoff mass balance already uses (outlet is a node, or the
subcatchment itself), as the patched legacy output.c does. Projects without
subcatchment-to-subcatchment routing are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-57_swmm600.patch

diff --git a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
index 839529d..934770c 100644
--- a/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
+++ b/src/engine/core/SWMMEngine.cpp
@@ -6631,7 +6631,11 @@ void SWMMEngine::postOutputSnapshot(double /*dt_step*/) noexcept {
                     }
                     a_infil += static_cast<float>(
                         static_cast<float>(snap.subcatch.infil[ui]) * area);
-                    a_runoff += static_cast<float>(snap.subcatch.runoff[ui]);
+                    // Runoff sent onto another subcatchment is counted there
+                    // (the runoff mass balance's rule, legacy output.c).
+                    if (ctx_.subcatches.outlet_node[ui] >= 0 ||
+                        ctx_.subcatches.outlet_subcatch[ui] == i)
+                        a_runoff += static_cast<float>(snap.subcatch.runoff[ui]);
                 }
                 if (total_area > 0.0) {
                     a_evap  /= total_area;
